  ["Fishing"]={
    name="Fishing",
    page_url="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Category:Fishing",
    recipes_url="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Category:Fishing/All_Fish",
    primary_guide_id="wiki_7265",
    primary_guide_title="Fishing Like a Pro 1-100 by Pepen",
    ranges={
      ["0-10"]={ rank="Amateur", url="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Category:Fishing/Amateur", blocks={
        "0-11\010\010Crayfish (7), Any Rod, Little Worm Most Freshwater bodies, I'd recommend catching these at Knightswell in West Ronfaure You can catch these while you get Moat Carp at the same time. Crayfish have limited uses outside of early cooking skill ups.\010Moat Carp (11) Hume Fishing Rod, Halcyon Rod, Insect Paste, West Ronfaure Knightswell- Same as above just with paste to isolate out the crayfish or use little worms if you don't mind getting crayfish too. Save all of your moat carp for Lu Shang's or sell on AH if you need gil. Save one for TEST ITEM\010Knightswell gets fished out constantly and is no longer the best place for Moat Carp.",
        "0-56\010\010Moat Carp (11) [[Hume Fishing Rod],Halcyon Rod, Insect Paste, West Ronfaure Knightswell- Keep one for TEST ITEM\010Tricolored Carp (27) [Hume Rod] Insect Paste Port San d'Oria- This set up will net you tricolored carp about 30% of the time and the rest will be Moat Carp and sometimes Gold Carp which may be hard to reel in so if you have trouble cancel them and any you do catch NPC.\010TEST ITEM Cheval Salmon (21) Buy from AH, it should be cheap.\010Nosteau Herring (39) Halcyon Rod, Sardine Balls, Lower Jeuno, Qufim Island- On the cliffside as you come out of the sea tunnel. Taking a break from Moat Carp to get within skill range of the next area, catch these to cap. -These are impossible to isolate from Tiger Cod which isn't a bad thing since they both sell quite well on the AH and for a nice profit compared to bait cost. If you have cooking close to 46 make them into Pickled Herrings and NPC for massive profits while you twirl your mustache with glee. I would recommend getting cooking to 13 and turning the Tiger Cod you catch into Sliced Cod To then NPC or sell on AH if that's more profitable but NPC should yield you about 5k per stack. Use all gil earned from this step to buy moat carp from the AH.\010TEST ITEM Gugru Tuna (41)- Buy off AH they're cheap and not worth the headache of catching yourself.\010Gold Carp (56) Halcyon Rod Insect Paste Windurst Woods- You will catch these as well as Moat Carp most of the time, NPC all Gold Carp for around ~300g each to buy more Moat Carp. Cap your skill here and you should have the 10,000 turned in by now or you should be very close. Once you have Lu Shang's please refer to the Lu Shang's section to continue.",
      }},
      ["11-20"]={ rank="Recruit", url="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Category:Fishing/Recruit", blocks={
        "0-11\010\010Crayfish (7), Any Rod, Little Worm Most Freshwater bodies, I'd recommend catching these at Knightswell in West Ronfaure You can catch these while you get Moat Carp at the same time. Crayfish have limited uses outside of early cooking skill ups.\010Moat Carp (11) Hume Fishing Rod, Halcyon Rod, Insect Paste, West Ronfaure Knightswell- Same as above just with paste to isolate out the crayfish or use little worms if you don't mind getting crayfish too. Save all of your moat carp for Lu Shang's or sell on AH if you need gil. Save one for TEST ITEM\010Knightswell gets fished out constantly and is no longer the best place for Moat Carp.",
        "11-27\010\010Yellow Globe (17) Halcyon Rod, Sabiki Rig, Mhaura OR Buburimu Peninsula- Caught by the truck loads with this set up in either zone, preferred Mhaura but if you find it over camped go to Buburimu instead. Used in alchemy for poison powder, sell on AH or NPC.\010Cheval Salmon (21) Halcyon Rod, Fly Lure East Ronfaure- Catch these just outside of Southern San d'oria in the stream until 18 or 20 if you prefer to stay here longer. Shining Trout will also bite here which may be difficult to reel in which is why I recommend you only stay here until 18. This is a TEST ITEM turn it in, NPC the rest and immediately head to the next target.\010Nebimonite (27) Halcyon Rod, Crayfish Ball/Shrimp Lure,Ship bound for Mhaura/Selbina- Ferry fishing can be a drag but catching these are very profitable even if crayfish balls are 6-7k per stack which is the bait I'd recommend although you CAN use the shrimp lure but it can hook fish that will break your rod/snap your line but you can cancel those, still not time efficient but figured I'd give an option. Fish these up til cap and sell on AH you should easily make the cost of bait back plus a nice profit. Fish on the stairs and angle your character diagonally to avoid the lower deck monsters if you are low level also have Sneak available too.\010TEST ITEM Giant Catfish Just buy this on the AH there should be plenty of stock.",
        "0-56\010\010Moat Carp (11) [[Hume Fishing Rod],Halcyon Rod, Insect Paste, West Ronfaure Knightswell- Keep one for TEST ITEM\010Tricolored Carp (27) [Hume Rod] Insect Paste Port San d'Oria- This set up will net you tricolored carp about 30% of the time and the rest will be Moat Carp and sometimes Gold Carp which may be hard to reel in so if you have trouble cancel them and any you do catch NPC.\010TEST ITEM Cheval Salmon (21) Buy from AH, it should be cheap.\010Nosteau Herring (39) Halcyon Rod, Sardine Balls, Lower Jeuno, Qufim Island- On the cliffside as you come out of the sea tunnel. Taking a break from Moat Carp to get within skill range of the next area, catch these to cap. -These are impossible to isolate from Tiger Cod which isn't a bad thing since they both sell quite well on the AH and for a nice profit compared to bait cost. If you have cooking close to 46 make them into Pickled Herrings and NPC for massive profits while you twirl your mustache with glee. I would recommend getting cooking to 13 and turning the Tiger Cod you catch into Sliced Cod To then NPC or sell on AH if that's more profitable but NPC should yield you about 5k per stack. Use all gil earned from this step to buy moat carp from the AH.\010TEST ITEM Gugru Tuna (41)- Buy off AH they're cheap and not worth the headache of catching yourself.\010Gold Carp (56) Halcyon Rod Insect Paste Windurst Woods- You will catch these as well as Moat Carp most of the time, NPC all Gold Carp for around ~300g each to buy more Moat Carp. Cap your skill here and you should have the 10,000 turned in by now or you should be very close. Once you have Lu Shang's please refer to the Lu Shang's section to continue.",
      }},
      ["21-30"]={ rank="Initiate", url="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Category:Fishing/Initiate", blocks={
        "11-27\010\010Yellow Globe (17) Halcyon Rod, Sabiki Rig, Mhaura OR Buburimu Peninsula- Caught by the truck loads with this set up in either zone, preferred Mhaura but if you find it over camped go to Buburimu instead. Used in alchemy for poison powder, sell on AH or NPC.\010Cheval Salmon (21) Halcyon Rod, Fly Lure East Ronfaure- Catch these just outside of Southern San d'oria in the stream until 18 or 20 if you prefer to stay here longer. Shining Trout will also bite here which may be difficult to reel in which is why I recommend you only stay here until 18. This is a TEST ITEM turn it in, NPC the rest and immediately head to the next target.\010Nebimonite (27) Halcyon Rod, Crayfish Ball/Shrimp Lure,Ship bound for Mhaura/Selbina- Ferry fishing can be a drag but catching these are very profitable even if crayfish balls are 6-7k per stack which is the bait I'd recommend although you CAN use the shrimp lure but it can hook fish that will break your rod/snap your line but you can cancel those, still not time efficient but figured I'd give an option. Fish these up til cap and sell on AH you should easily make the cost of bait back plus a nice profit. Fish on the stairs and angle your character diagonally to avoid the lower deck monsters if you are low level also have Sneak available too.\010TEST ITEM Giant Catfish Just buy this on the AH there should be plenty of stock.",
        "27-39\010\010Shining Trout (37) Halcyon Rod, Fly Lure, East Ronfaure- Same spot you caught the Cheval Salmon except now you can get those pesky trout easier. Fish these to cap and NPC everything or move on to the next fish instead.\010Nosteau Herring (39) Halcyon Rod, Sardine Balls, Lower Jeuno, Qufim Island- On the cliffside as you come out of the sea tunnel. -These are impossible to isolate from Tiger Cod which isn't a bad thing and I'd recommend you level cooking to 13 to turn these into sliced cod for better profit to sell to NPC. If you have cooking close to 46 make them into Pickled Herrings and NPC for massive profits while you twirl your mustache with glee.\010TEST ITEM Gugru Tuna (41)- Buy off AH they're cheap and not worth the headache of catching yourself.",
        "0-56\010\010Moat Carp (11) [[Hume Fishing Rod],Halcyon Rod, Insect Paste, West Ronfaure Knightswell- Keep one for TEST ITEM\010Tricolored Carp (27) [Hume Rod] Insect Paste Port San d'Oria- This set up will net you tricolored carp about 30% of the time and the rest will be Moat Carp and sometimes Gold Carp which may be hard to reel in so if you have trouble cancel them and any you do catch NPC.\010TEST ITEM Cheval Salmon (21) Buy from AH, it should be cheap.\010Nosteau Herring (39) Halcyon Rod, Sardine Balls, Lower Jeuno, Qufim Island- On the cliffside as you come out of the sea tunnel. Taking a break from Moat Carp to get within skill range of the next area, catch these to cap. -These are impossible to isolate from Tiger Cod which isn't a bad thing since they both sell quite well on the AH and for a nice profit compared to bait cost. If you have cooking close to 46 make them into Pickled Herrings and NPC for massive profits while you twirl your mustache with glee. I would recommend getting cooking to 13 and turning the Tiger Cod you catch into Sliced Cod To then NPC or sell on AH if that's more profitable but NPC should yield you about 5k per stack. Use all gil earned from this step to buy moat carp from the AH.\010TEST ITEM Gugru Tuna (41)- Buy off AH they're cheap and not worth the headache of catching yourself.\010Gold Carp (56) Halcyon Rod Insect Paste Windurst Woods- You will catch these as well as Moat Carp most of the time, NPC all Gold Carp for around ~300g each to buy more Moat Carp. Cap your skill here and you should have the 10,000 turned in by now or you should be very close. Once you have Lu Shang's please refer to the Lu Shang's section to continue.",
      }},
      ["31-40"]={ rank="Novice", url="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Category:Fishing/Novice", blocks={
        "27-39\010\010Shining Trout (37) Halcyon Rod, Fly Lure, East Ronfaure- Same spot you caught the Cheval Salmon except now you can get those pesky trout easier. Fish these to cap and NPC everything or move on to the next fish instead.\010Nosteau Herring (39) Halcyon Rod, Sardine Balls, Lower Jeuno, Qufim Island- On the cliffside as you come out of the sea tunnel. -These are impossible to isolate from Tiger Cod which isn't a bad thing and I'd recommend you level cooking to 13 to turn these into sliced cod for better profit to sell to NPC. If you have cooking close to 46 make them into Pickled Herrings and NPC for massive profits while you twirl your mustache with glee.\010TEST ITEM Gugru Tuna (41)- Buy off AH they're cheap and not worth the headache of catching yourself.",
        "39-61\010\010Cone Calamary (48) Halcyon Rod, Minnow, Batallia Downs- These will NPC pretty well and you'll also catch some Bluetail with this set up at the same time although you may lose some of them to \"lack of skill\" messages but nevertheless it's still worth your time as you'll grow into catching them here soon enough and the NPC profits start to get kind of crazy here.\010TEST ITEM: Monke-Onke- Buy off AH shouldn't be expensive\010Bluetail (55) Halcyon Rod, Minnow, Qufim Island The ice pond. This set up will isolate out the cone calamary and all of the other nasty fish that will break your rod/line. Fish these up until cap they NPC for 300g each and will be your primary target toward buying the moat carp for the Lu Shang's quest.\010Bhefhel Marlin (61) Mithran Fishing Rod/Composite Fishing Rod, Slice of Bluetail, Ship bound for Mhaura/Selbina- I decided to add these because I don't think they are too much trouble to catch but have been reported to break Halcyon Rods and Hume Rods. That could be a bonus if you're in the market of repairing broken rods with Alchemy or Woodworking. This combination will also target Cone Calamary as well as Silver Shark although you may or may not have difficulties catching them. These will be the \" | !\" bites you have chance at reeling in, the others will be legendary fish that will snap your line or break your rod and will be impossible to reel in so cancel those. These could also be a decent target to grind for your Lu Shang's Rod because they sell quickly for 2.5k each on the AH at the time of writing but your mileage may vary. Used for Inside the Belly for Pirate's Chart Quest TEST ITEM",
        "0-56\010\010Moat Carp (11) [[Hume Fishing Rod],Halcyon Rod, Insect Paste, West Ronfaure Knightswell- Keep one for TEST ITEM\010Tricolored Carp (27) [Hume Rod] Insect Paste Port San d'Oria- This set up will net you tricolored carp about 30% of the time and the rest will be Moat Carp and sometimes Gold Carp which may be hard to reel in so if you have trouble cancel them and any you do catch NPC.\010TEST ITEM Cheval Salmon (21) Buy from AH, it should be cheap.\010Nosteau Herring (39) Halcyon Rod, Sardine Balls, Lower Jeuno, Qufim Island- On the cliffside as you come out of the sea tunnel. Taking a break from Moat Carp to get within skill range of the next area, catch these to cap. -These are impossible to isolate from Tiger Cod which isn't a bad thing since they both sell quite well on the AH and for a nice profit compared to bait cost. If you have cooking close to 46 make them into Pickled Herrings and NPC for massive profits while you twirl your mustache with glee. I would recommend getting cooking to 13 and turning the Tiger Cod you catch into Sliced Cod To then NPC or sell on AH if that's more profitable but NPC should yield you about 5k per stack. Use all gil earned from this step to buy moat carp from the AH.\010TEST ITEM Gugru Tuna (41)- Buy off AH they're cheap and not worth the headache of catching yourself.\010Gold Carp (56) Halcyon Rod Insect Paste Windurst Woods- You will catch these as well as Moat Carp most of the time, NPC all Gold Carp for around ~300g each to buy more Moat Carp. Cap your skill here and you should have the 10,000 turned in by now or you should be very close. Once you have Lu Shang's please refer to the Lu Shang's section to continue.",
      }},
